      "code": "memcpy(&closure->func, func, sizeof(zend_internal_function));",
      "note": "Root cause fixed by the patch. Internal closure creation copies the borrowed `function_name` pointer from `func` into the closure without incrementing the underlying `zend_string` refcount, so multiple closures can later release the same allocation as though each owned it. The patch adds the missing `zend_string_addref(closure->func.op_array.function_name);` in this branch and then balances temporary trampoline wrappers with explicit releases after closure creation.",
